1
00:00:09,510 --> 00:00:11,320
Later, I looked around the area.

2
00:00:11,350 --> 00:00:12,560
There was no one else around.

3
00:00:13,030 --> 00:00:15,590
I wanted to see
if Liang Chao was really dead.

4
00:00:15,590 --> 00:00:18,030
But when I went back to that room,

5
00:00:18,160 --> 00:00:19,920
something strange had happened.

6
00:00:57,520 --> 00:00:59,280
Liang Chao had simply vanished.

7
00:00:59,710 --> 00:01:00,710
It was Zhao Qian.

8
00:01:01,240 --> 00:01:03,110
Zhao Qian must have killed him.

9
00:01:03,110 --> 00:01:04,350
Let them turn on each other.

10
00:01:04,870 --> 00:01:06,310
Every one of them deserves it.

11
00:01:06,510 --> 00:01:07,310
Zhao Qian?

12
00:01:08,590 --> 00:01:12,310
Are you sure
you saw Zhao Qian that night?

13
00:01:12,510 --> 00:01:14,510
I'd recognize him
even if he were reduced to ashes.

14
00:01:15,840 --> 00:01:18,120
He was the bookkeeper
for those scammers.

15
00:01:18,120 --> 00:01:20,280
How did all the money
we worked so hard to invest disappear?

16
00:01:20,280 --> 00:01:22,350
How did it end up in their own pockets?

17
00:01:22,350 --> 00:01:23,680
Every cent went through his hands.

18
00:01:23,680 --> 00:01:25,870
Every calculation he made

19
00:01:26,070 --> 00:01:27,840
was with our life savings.

20
00:01:29,980 --> 00:01:33,980
=Medical Examiner Dr. Qin: Bones of the Past=
=Episode 15=

21
00:01:35,840 --> 00:01:37,400
What kind of person is Zhao Qian

22
00:01:37,400 --> 00:01:38,590
from your finance department?

23
00:01:39,950 --> 00:01:41,070
How should I put it?

24
00:01:41,280 --> 00:01:42,640
He's basically

25
00:01:43,640 --> 00:01:45,000
someone no one can control.

26
00:01:45,640 --> 00:01:47,950
Zhao Qian is Mr. Huo's cousin.

27
00:01:48,200 --> 00:01:50,230
Mr. Huo put him
in the finance department

28
00:01:50,230 --> 00:01:51,950
to keep an eye on things for him.

29
00:01:52,200 --> 00:01:53,350
Ms. Liu knew that perfectly well,

30
00:01:53,350 --> 00:01:54,680
so she never really tried to manage him.

31
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:57,200
Zhao Qian was constantly skipping work,

32
00:01:57,400 --> 00:01:58,640
and she just turned a blind eye.

33
00:01:58,710 --> 00:01:59,710
What about Mr. Liang?

34
00:02:00,120 --> 00:02:01,150
How did he react?

35
00:02:01,310 --> 00:02:02,200
Mr. Liang?

36
00:02:02,400 --> 00:02:04,040
Mr. Liang couldn't stand Zhao Qian.

37
00:02:04,070 --> 00:02:06,560
He thought Zhao Qian was incompetent
and only got by on connections.

38
00:02:07,230 --> 00:02:10,520
Once, Mr. Liang
said right in front of Ms. Liu,

39
00:02:10,870 --> 00:02:12,240
"Zhao Qian skipped work again.

40
00:02:12,240 --> 00:02:13,360
Aren't you going
to do something about it?"

41
00:02:13,360 --> 00:02:15,150
Ms. Liu only said,

42
00:02:15,560 --> 00:02:19,240
"Mr. Huo knows
what's going on with Zhao Qian."

43
00:02:19,470 --> 00:02:21,150
After that, Mr. Liang said nothing.

44
00:02:21,360 --> 00:02:24,240
Zhao Qian
had Mr. Huo backing him, after all.

45
00:02:26,520 --> 00:02:29,560
Does Zhao Qian
have any distinguishing features?

46
00:02:33,750 --> 00:02:34,870
I just remembered.

47
00:02:35,120 --> 00:02:36,840
Mr. Liang mentioned something
about him before.

48
00:02:39,030 --> 00:02:39,840
Where's Zhao Qian?

49
00:02:41,430 --> 00:02:43,120
He said he went to
the hospital to pick up his medicine.

50
00:02:46,800 --> 00:02:48,680
Someone who can't even
read an income statement

51
00:02:48,680 --> 00:02:50,080
sits in the finance department every day

52
00:02:50,520 --> 00:02:51,680
and gets paid more than anyone else.

53
00:02:54,240 --> 00:02:55,710
Mr. Liang, keep your voice down.

54
00:02:57,630 --> 00:02:59,150
Even Ms. Liu
doesn't dare interfere with him.

55
00:02:59,430 --> 00:03:00,240
We...

56
00:03:01,030 --> 00:03:02,430
You think Liu Yan can control him?

57
00:03:03,590 --> 00:03:06,000
I'm telling you,
if Liu Yan ever says no,

58
00:03:08,120 --> 00:03:09,630
Mr. Huo will hear about it immediately.

59
00:03:09,630 --> 00:03:11,430
All she can do is turn a blind eye.

60
00:03:14,400 --> 00:03:17,190
So what's actually wrong with him?

61
00:03:21,150 --> 00:03:23,150
Someone who goes
to places like that every day,

62
00:03:23,430 --> 00:03:24,520
what do you think
could be wrong with him?

63
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:28,750
Later, when something
happened to the group,

64
00:03:28,800 --> 00:03:30,150
Mr. Huo went into hiding.

65
00:03:30,280 --> 00:03:31,910
Zhao Qian no longer
had anyone protecting him.

66
00:03:31,910 --> 00:03:33,080
That day,

67
00:03:33,910 --> 00:03:36,310
Mr. Liang suddenly stormed into
the finance department with two men

68
00:03:36,360 --> 00:03:37,630
and insisted on taking the company seal.

69
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:40,120
Ms. Liu hid in the restroom
and wouldn't come out.

70
00:03:40,630 --> 00:03:41,430
Zhao Qian...

71
00:03:42,150 --> 00:03:43,560
Zhao Qian happened to be there too,

72
00:03:43,590 --> 00:03:45,240
but he refused to hand over
the company seal.

73
00:03:45,310 --> 00:03:47,470
Mr. Liang yanked him out of his chair

74
00:03:47,800 --> 00:03:49,520
and cursed him
out for about ten minutes.

75
00:03:50,120 --> 00:03:51,750
He insulted his entire family.

76
00:03:51,750 --> 00:03:52,710
Did he hit him?

77
00:03:54,120 --> 00:03:55,280
He slapped him twice.

78
00:03:55,590 --> 00:03:57,120
Zhao Qian's lip was even bleeding.

79
00:03:57,120 --> 00:03:58,000
Mr. Liang said,

80
00:03:58,280 --> 00:03:59,630
"Aren't you so cocky because you have
your cousin backing you?

81
00:03:59,630 --> 00:04:00,430
Where is he now?

82
00:04:00,560 --> 00:04:02,470
Now that he's gone, what are you?"

83
00:04:02,800 --> 00:04:04,000
How did Zhao Qian react?

84
00:04:04,080 --> 00:04:04,870
He said,

85
00:04:04,870 --> 00:04:06,960
"Liang Chao,
I'm the only one you dare hit.

86
00:04:07,590 --> 00:04:10,190
Can you honestly say you didn't take
a cent of my cousin's money?"

87
00:04:10,190 --> 00:04:11,000
What happened next?

88
00:04:11,150 --> 00:04:13,520
Then Mr. Liang
froze for a couple of seconds.

89
00:04:13,520 --> 00:04:14,630
Then he kicked him again.

90
00:04:14,870 --> 00:04:16,750
He grabbed the company seal and left.

91
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:18,430
Before leaving, he also said,

92
00:04:18,870 --> 00:04:20,120
"Starting today,

93
00:04:20,270 --> 00:04:22,040
you're no longer
part of the Urban Construction Group."

94
00:04:22,160 --> 00:04:24,040
Did Zhao Qian
come back to work after that?

95
00:04:24,360 --> 00:04:25,920
I don't think he came in the next day.

96
00:04:26,040 --> 00:04:28,270
I heard he was hospitalized.

97
00:04:28,630 --> 00:04:29,920
I never saw him again.

98
00:04:32,430 --> 00:04:33,310
Listen,

99
00:04:33,950 --> 00:04:35,830
according to Zhang Daxin's account,

100
00:04:36,040 --> 00:04:38,560
the fingerprints
and footprints left at the scene

101
00:04:38,950 --> 00:04:40,190
were all made after he entered the scene

102
00:04:40,190 --> 00:04:41,800
and touched things and walked around.

103
00:04:41,830 --> 00:04:43,190
This circumstantial evidence

104
00:04:43,510 --> 00:04:45,270
isn't enough to prove he's the killer.

105
00:04:47,160 --> 00:04:49,120
Could he have been lying to us?

106
00:04:49,240 --> 00:04:51,720
Maybe he used the bad blood
between Zhao Qian and Liang Chao

107
00:04:51,720 --> 00:04:53,630
to make up a story no one could verify.

108
00:04:53,630 --> 00:04:54,830
He was the killer.

109
00:04:54,950 --> 00:04:56,800
He made up the story
about Zhao Qian killing Liang Chao

110
00:04:56,800 --> 00:04:57,630
to muddy the waters

111
00:04:57,630 --> 00:04:58,430
and throw us off.

112
00:04:58,430 --> 00:04:59,560
That's possible.

113
00:04:59,720 --> 00:05:01,190
So we need to find Zhao Qian
as soon as possible.

114
00:05:01,750 --> 00:05:03,680
Once we compare their statements,
we'll know the truth.

115
00:05:07,040 --> 00:05:07,830
Qin,

116
00:05:08,390 --> 00:05:09,190
I heard

117
00:05:09,190 --> 00:05:11,000
Criminal Investigation has been looking
into Zhao Qian lately too.

118
00:05:12,160 --> 00:05:12,950
What's going on?

119
00:05:13,830 --> 00:05:15,360
We've actually had our eye
on him for a long time.

120
00:05:15,360 --> 00:05:15,950
Listen,

121
00:05:15,950 --> 00:05:16,600
this Zhao Qian

122
00:05:16,600 --> 00:05:18,190
was actually an accountant for
the Longfan Urban Construction Group.

123
00:05:18,190 --> 00:05:20,430
He's said to be Huo Qicheng's cousin.

124
00:05:20,600 --> 00:05:22,040
Huo Qicheng trusted him deeply.

125
00:05:22,070 --> 00:05:23,070
He handled quite
a few things for Huo Qicheng

126
00:05:23,070 --> 00:05:23,870
and had plenty of connections.

127
00:05:25,600 --> 00:05:26,750
Have you summoned him for questioning?

128
00:05:26,800 --> 00:05:27,600
No.

129
00:05:28,040 --> 00:05:29,720
That's exactly what I came to tell you.

130
00:05:29,920 --> 00:05:31,240
When we were given our instructions,

131
00:05:31,240 --> 00:05:33,190
we were told to secretly investigate
the key figures in the fundraising fraud case.

132
00:05:33,510 --> 00:05:34,750
That's when I noticed
something was off about him.

133
00:05:34,750 --> 00:05:35,800
After Huo Qicheng died,

134
00:05:35,800 --> 00:05:37,240
he became as skittish
as a frightened rabbit.

135
00:05:37,240 --> 00:05:39,240
He basically stayed holed up
at home and rarely went out.

136
00:05:39,310 --> 00:05:40,270
After Jin Juan died,

137
00:05:40,270 --> 00:05:41,560
we planned to formally
summon him for questioning,

138
00:05:41,560 --> 00:05:42,510
but he'd already disappeared.

139
00:05:43,600 --> 00:05:44,680
If that's the case,

140
00:05:45,430 --> 00:05:47,430
Zhao Qian has
been missing for quite a while.

141
00:05:50,270 --> 00:05:51,070
Li,

142
00:05:51,920 --> 00:05:52,720
tomorrow,

143
00:05:53,950 --> 00:05:55,430
based on what we know,

144
00:05:55,430 --> 00:05:57,270
go over Zhao Qian's

145
00:05:57,270 --> 00:05:58,310
connections again.

146
00:05:58,630 --> 00:06:00,750
Talk to whoever needs to be interviewed
and investigate whatever needs checking.

147
00:06:00,920 --> 00:06:01,870
Find him as soon as possible.

148
00:06:01,870 --> 00:06:02,390
All right.

149
00:06:06,830 --> 00:06:07,510
I'm done eating.

150
00:06:07,510 --> 00:06:09,190
There's half an egg left.
Have it if you want.

151
00:06:09,240 --> 00:06:10,120
Not eating anymore?

152
00:06:11,390 --> 00:06:12,160
Don't go yet.

153
00:06:12,160 --> 00:06:13,480
Stay and chat a little longer.

154
00:06:14,040 --> 00:06:14,800
See?

155
00:06:15,040 --> 00:06:16,270
My wife, your brother,

156
00:06:16,270 --> 00:06:17,870
I've got a whole family waiting for me.

157
00:06:18,270 --> 00:06:19,720
I don't even want
to waste another minute talking to you.

158
00:06:24,480 --> 00:06:25,270
Son.

159
00:06:39,310 --> 00:06:41,600
Do you remember what Mr. Know-It-All

160
00:06:41,720 --> 00:06:42,630
told you that day?

161
00:06:43,830 --> 00:06:45,510
Mr. Know-It-All?

162
00:06:46,600 --> 00:06:48,720
He told me a lot of things,

163
00:06:48,800 --> 00:06:50,390
but I can't remember them clearly.

164
00:06:50,390 --> 00:06:53,510
Anyway, he said if I listened to him,
I could save Dad.

165
00:06:53,750 --> 00:06:55,000
And I did it.

166
00:06:55,240 --> 00:06:57,120
Dad, wasn't I amazing?

167
00:07:01,870 --> 00:07:02,680
You're awake.

168
00:07:04,120 --> 00:07:04,950
You're off work.

169
00:07:06,630 --> 00:07:07,430
How are you?

170
00:07:08,390 --> 00:07:09,270
Is everything okay?

171
00:07:09,630 --> 00:07:10,480
Everything's fine.

172
00:07:16,750 --> 00:07:18,070
I was so worried.

173
00:07:19,390 --> 00:07:22,040
I fell asleep just now
and dreamed something happened to you.

174
00:07:22,040 --> 00:07:23,630
Don't always put yourself in danger.

175
00:07:23,630 --> 00:07:24,920
Ming and I can't live without you.

176
00:07:24,920 --> 00:07:25,750
Do you understand?

177
00:07:25,870 --> 00:07:27,390
Haven't I told you before?

178
00:07:27,390 --> 00:07:30,680
The three of us will always be together.

179
00:07:31,270 --> 00:07:32,070
As for me,

180
00:07:32,680 --> 00:07:35,600
my job for the rest of my life
is to protect you and our son.

181
00:07:37,430 --> 00:07:38,310
It's a promise.

182
00:07:38,390 --> 00:07:39,190
Of course.

183
00:07:39,920 --> 00:07:41,190
Let's go home. Come on.

184
00:07:41,750 --> 00:07:42,510
Wait.

185
00:07:44,600 --> 00:07:46,270
Did you eat instant noodles again?

186
00:07:47,680 --> 00:07:49,600
Didn't I tell you

187
00:07:49,800 --> 00:07:50,950
to eat less instant noodles?

188
00:07:50,950 --> 00:07:52,240
They're bad for your stomach.

189
00:07:52,240 --> 00:07:54,120
Li practically forced me to eat them.

190
00:07:55,120 --> 00:07:56,390
Then promise me.

191
00:07:57,680 --> 00:07:58,600
I won't eat it anymore.

192
00:07:59,510 --> 00:08:00,510
Then can you

193
00:08:01,160 --> 00:08:02,630
promise me something too?

194
00:08:03,360 --> 00:08:04,270
Go ahead.

195
00:08:04,510 --> 00:08:05,560
From now on,

196
00:08:06,920 --> 00:08:08,310
could our family

197
00:08:09,800 --> 00:08:11,190
have dumpling
a little less often each month?

198
00:08:11,190 --> 00:08:12,480
They're awful.

199
00:08:12,830 --> 00:08:13,510
Get lost.

200
00:08:13,680 --> 00:08:14,310
I'm never

201
00:08:14,310 --> 00:08:15,600
cooking anything for you again.

202
00:08:15,720 --> 00:08:16,870
Come on, let's go home.

203
00:08:17,190 --> 00:08:17,680
Let's go.

204
00:08:17,680 --> 00:08:18,750
We're going home.

205
00:08:18,750 --> 00:08:19,240
Come on.

206
00:08:21,190 --> 00:08:22,000
Let's go.

207
00:08:23,430 --> 00:08:24,190
Slow down.

208
00:08:24,190 --> 00:08:25,070
Jump!

209
00:08:42,480 --> 00:08:44,460
Ming, you're back.

210
00:08:45,270 --> 00:08:46,390
Mom, did I wake you?

211
00:08:46,390 --> 00:08:47,120
No.

212
00:08:47,560 --> 00:08:48,550
I was waiting for you to come home.

213
00:08:48,670 --> 00:08:50,200
You've been so busy these past few days.

214
00:08:50,390 --> 00:08:51,240
Everything okay?

215
00:08:51,510 --> 00:08:52,320
I'm fine.

216
00:08:53,200 --> 00:08:55,200
Come here. I have something to tell you.

217
00:09:05,030 --> 00:09:05,840
Ming,

218
00:09:07,240 --> 00:09:10,000
there's something I've wanted
to tell you for a long time.

219
00:09:11,160 --> 00:09:13,000
Back then, whenever your dad
went out on a case,

220
00:09:13,530 --> 00:09:14,750
I may have looked calm,

221
00:09:14,870 --> 00:09:16,870
but I was always worried sick inside.

222
00:09:17,080 --> 00:09:18,240
But I wanted to support him,

223
00:09:19,720 --> 00:09:20,630
so I never dared say anything.

224
00:09:20,960 --> 00:09:22,150
After your dad passed away,

225
00:09:22,240 --> 00:09:23,320
I became even more afraid.

226
00:09:23,870 --> 00:09:25,150
When you applied to the police academy,

227
00:09:25,600 --> 00:09:27,440
every part of me was against it.

228
00:09:27,720 --> 00:09:29,080
Your dad and I
had already spent enough time

229
00:09:29,080 --> 00:09:30,790
living in constant fear.

230
00:09:31,840 --> 00:09:33,360
I didn't want to lose you too.

231
00:09:34,480 --> 00:09:35,270
Mom,

232
00:09:37,720 --> 00:09:38,510
I know.

233
00:09:39,390 --> 00:09:40,870
I'll take good care of myself.

234
00:09:41,840 --> 00:09:42,630
I know.

235
00:09:43,110 --> 00:09:44,440
You're just like your dad.

236
00:09:45,270 --> 00:09:47,960
Once you've made up your mind,
no one can stop you.

237
00:09:48,670 --> 00:09:49,910
I thought about it for a long time

238
00:09:50,480 --> 00:09:51,840
and finally gave you my blessing.

239
00:09:52,910 --> 00:09:54,670
I've stayed by your side all these years

240
00:09:55,270 --> 00:09:56,670
because it was the only way

241
00:09:57,120 --> 00:09:58,510
I could feel that you were safe.

242
00:10:02,480 --> 00:10:03,480
Looking back now,

243
00:10:04,480 --> 00:10:05,720
I was too anxious

244
00:10:07,440 --> 00:10:08,750
and didn't give you enough space.

245
00:10:09,870 --> 00:10:10,870
I've come to terms with it.

246
00:10:11,680 --> 00:10:12,820
It's time for me to let go.

247
00:10:15,550 --> 00:10:16,720
I wanted to let you know

248
00:10:17,320 --> 00:10:19,000
that I'm thinking
of moving back to our old place.

249
00:10:19,720 --> 00:10:21,960
That's where your dad and I
made our happiest memories.

250
00:10:23,030 --> 00:10:25,150
It's also close to the hospital,
so it's convenient.

251
00:10:27,030 --> 00:10:27,840
Mom,

252
00:10:30,030 --> 00:10:31,120
let's find a time when I'm off

253
00:10:31,510 --> 00:10:32,550
and I'll go take a look with you.

254
00:10:33,790 --> 00:10:34,600
All right.

255
00:10:35,030 --> 00:10:35,790
There's soup in the pot.

256
00:10:36,030 --> 00:10:37,080
I'll get you some.

257
00:10:46,150 --> 00:10:47,910
We got to come home
with Dad after work today.

258
00:10:47,910 --> 00:10:48,720
Are you happy?

259
00:10:48,720 --> 00:10:49,200
Yes.

260
00:10:49,200 --> 00:10:50,360
- Let's go back and watch Flower Fairy.
- Captain Qin.

261
00:10:50,440 --> 00:10:51,240
Doctor Lin.

262
00:10:51,360 --> 00:10:53,030
You're finally back.

263
00:10:53,030 --> 00:10:54,150
I've been waiting for you for ages.

264
00:10:54,150 --> 00:10:54,510
What happened?

265
00:10:54,510 --> 00:10:57,030
Your door was forced open.

266
00:10:57,240 --> 00:10:58,030
The neighbors said

267
00:10:58,030 --> 00:10:59,630
they saw someone acting suspiciously

268
00:10:59,670 --> 00:11:00,870
outside your door.

269
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:01,960
Our neighborhood

270
00:11:01,960 --> 00:11:03,390
has always been very safe.

271
00:11:03,550 --> 00:11:04,840
We've never had a break-in before.

272
00:11:04,960 --> 00:11:08,240
And the first time it happens,
they target a police officer's home.

273
00:11:08,240 --> 00:11:09,510
Mrs. Huang, don't worry.

274
00:11:09,790 --> 00:11:10,720
I'll go inside and take a look.

275
00:11:12,030 --> 00:11:13,120
Thank you, Mrs. Huang.

276
00:11:13,390 --> 00:11:14,200
No need to thank me.

277
00:11:14,440 --> 00:11:15,550
You two, a police officer and a doctor,

278
00:11:15,550 --> 00:11:16,840
have helped us plenty over the years.

279
00:11:17,030 --> 00:11:18,440
It's only right for neighbors
to look out for each other.

280
00:11:19,080 --> 00:11:20,320
Go check if anything's missing.

281
00:11:20,320 --> 00:11:21,320
I'll head home now.

282
00:11:21,320 --> 00:11:22,440
Thank you for your trouble, Mrs. Huang.

283
00:11:22,510 --> 00:11:23,720
You should get some rest.

284
00:11:23,720 --> 00:11:24,600
Go on.

285
00:11:24,600 --> 00:11:25,840
What's going on, Qin?

286
00:11:26,480 --> 00:11:27,630
- Is anything missing?
- It's fine.

287
00:11:27,870 --> 00:11:28,550
Nothing's wrong.

288
00:11:29,320 --> 00:11:30,270
It's just the door.

289
00:11:30,750 --> 00:11:32,360
A burglar probably forced it open.

290
00:11:32,360 --> 00:11:33,240
I'm guessing the burglar

291
00:11:33,240 --> 00:11:34,440
opened the door, took one look,

292
00:11:34,440 --> 00:11:35,200
and realized,

293
00:11:35,270 --> 00:11:36,440
we were even poorer than he was.

294
00:11:36,440 --> 00:11:37,720
So he decided to spare us

295
00:11:37,720 --> 00:11:38,440
and left.

296
00:11:38,550 --> 00:11:40,600
How can you
still joke at a time like this?

297
00:11:41,480 --> 00:11:43,120
Could someone
be trying to get back at you?

298
00:11:43,120 --> 00:11:43,840
How could that be?

299
00:11:43,840 --> 00:11:45,270
I'm the captain
of the Criminal Investigation Detachment.

300
00:11:45,600 --> 00:11:47,030
I've got Li and the whole team under me.

301
00:11:47,030 --> 00:11:47,670
All right.

302
00:11:48,200 --> 00:11:50,270
If anything happens, call the bureau.

303
00:11:50,360 --> 00:11:51,720
There are plenty
of neighbors around too.

304
00:11:51,840 --> 00:11:52,600
All right.

305
00:11:52,600 --> 00:11:53,320
Ming,

306
00:11:53,550 --> 00:11:55,320
from now on,
when Mom and Dad aren't home,

307
00:11:55,360 --> 00:11:57,600
you stay with Mrs. Huang.

308
00:11:57,670 --> 00:11:58,790
You're not allowed to stay home alone.

309
00:11:58,790 --> 00:11:59,600
Do you understand?

310
00:12:00,270 --> 00:12:01,630
You can only come home with us

311
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:03,270
when we come back to get you.

312
00:12:03,270 --> 00:12:03,960
Yes!

313
00:12:04,360 --> 00:12:05,600
Come on. Let's go take a shower.

314
00:12:05,670 --> 00:12:06,480
Okay.

315
00:12:08,630 --> 00:12:09,670
Be good, Ming.

316
00:12:10,200 --> 00:12:11,550
I know, Dad.

317
00:12:29,550 --> 00:12:30,360
Ming?

318
00:12:32,960 --> 00:12:33,790
Are you there, Ming?

319
00:13:07,740 --> 00:13:10,740
(Longfan City Department Store)

320
00:13:20,440 --> 00:13:22,360
Captain Qin,
there's been another incident.

321
00:13:22,790 --> 00:13:23,840
When was it discovered?

322
00:13:23,870 --> 00:13:24,720
This morning.

323
00:13:24,720 --> 00:13:26,790
Some fishermen nearby
were retrieving their nets

324
00:13:26,790 --> 00:13:29,200
when they spotted a partially
submerged box floating on the water.

325
00:13:29,320 --> 00:13:30,870
They thought
there might be valuables inside.

326
00:13:30,870 --> 00:13:31,550
But after they pulled it out,

327
00:13:31,550 --> 00:13:33,080
they found a body inside.

328
00:13:33,720 --> 00:13:34,870
Guess who the victim is.

329
00:13:35,080 --> 00:13:35,870
Who?

330
00:13:35,910 --> 00:13:37,320
Zhao Qian
from the Urban Construction Group.

331
00:13:50,670 --> 00:13:51,600
Are you sure it's Zhao Qian?

332
00:13:51,600 --> 00:13:52,360
Yes.

333
00:13:52,510 --> 00:13:53,360
Time of death?

334
00:13:53,440 --> 00:13:55,000
At least twelve hours ago.

335
00:13:55,840 --> 00:13:57,720
The box was submerged for too long.

336
00:13:57,720 --> 00:13:58,600
Any clues that might have been on it

337
00:13:58,600 --> 00:13:59,790
are probably gone by now.

338
00:13:59,790 --> 00:14:01,240
We didn't find anything either.

339
00:14:09,720 --> 00:14:10,510
Zhou,

340
00:14:10,550 --> 00:14:11,790
send it to the Technical Unit first.

341
00:14:11,790 --> 00:14:12,550
Once it's dried,

342
00:14:12,550 --> 00:14:13,750
we might be able to find

343
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:15,600
something useful on the tape.

344
00:14:17,550 --> 00:14:18,270
Step back.

345
00:14:18,270 --> 00:14:19,670
Don't contaminate the body.

346
00:14:20,080 --> 00:14:21,440
Zhenzhen, start taking notes.

347
00:14:21,440 --> 00:14:21,870
Okay.

348
00:14:21,870 --> 00:14:23,480
We need to break
the rigor mortis as soon as possible.

349
00:14:23,480 --> 00:14:25,910
If the body stays curled up like this

350
00:14:25,910 --> 00:14:28,270
until rigor mortis reaches its peak,
it'll be difficult to handle.

351
00:14:28,630 --> 00:14:30,390
It's exactly eight in the morning.

352
00:14:30,390 --> 00:14:31,480
Let's begin.

353
00:14:33,360 --> 00:14:34,150
Zhou,

354
00:14:34,630 --> 00:14:35,630
why did you just...

355
00:14:35,630 --> 00:14:36,630
Speak normally.

356
00:14:37,720 --> 00:14:39,510
I said, why did you
note the time just now?

357
00:14:39,510 --> 00:14:42,080
You need to compare
the body's current condition

358
00:14:42,390 --> 00:14:44,840
with the current time to determine

359
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:48,360
the exact time of death.

360
00:14:49,320 --> 00:14:50,270
It's really that stiff?

361
00:14:50,270 --> 00:14:51,510
Li, you don't understand, do you?

362
00:14:51,870 --> 00:14:53,790
This is the body speaking to us.

363
00:14:53,960 --> 00:14:55,750
Rigor mortis reaches its peak

364
00:14:55,750 --> 00:14:58,200
fifteen to seventeen hours after death.

365
00:14:58,200 --> 00:15:00,030
So Zhao Qian's time of death

366
00:15:00,030 --> 00:15:02,790
should have been sometime
yesterday afternoon or evening.

367
00:15:02,790 --> 00:15:03,360
Record that.

368
00:15:03,360 --> 00:15:04,000
Okay.

369
00:15:06,550 --> 00:15:08,120
The head suffered a heavy blow.

370
00:15:08,440 --> 00:15:09,630
Probably from a hammer.

371
00:15:10,360 --> 00:15:11,270
A hammer again?

372
00:15:11,270 --> 00:15:13,630
But it was probably
inflicted after death.

373
00:15:13,720 --> 00:15:14,910
There's no vital reaction.

374
00:15:15,080 --> 00:15:17,870
Besides multiple wounds
on the surface of the body,

375
00:15:17,870 --> 00:15:19,750
there's also
extensive subcutaneous hemorrhage.

376
00:15:21,080 --> 00:15:22,790
There are more than
a dozen similar wounds

377
00:15:22,790 --> 00:15:24,910
on the waist, abdomen, and outer thighs.

378
00:15:24,910 --> 00:15:27,480
Could these wounds be fatal?

379
00:15:28,630 --> 00:15:29,510
Something's not right.

380
00:15:29,870 --> 00:15:32,000
These wounds clearly only extend
into the subcutaneous tissue,

381
00:15:32,320 --> 00:15:34,320
but they look inflamed.

382
00:15:35,720 --> 00:15:36,510
Magnifying glass.

383
00:15:39,960 --> 00:15:42,440
The edges
of the wounds are all irregular,

384
00:15:43,120 --> 00:15:46,270
and there's about five millimeters
of dark yellow discoloration.

385
00:15:46,270 --> 00:15:48,360
The wounds
and wound surfaces are also yellow.

386
00:15:48,360 --> 00:15:50,120
Could these be skin ulcers?

387
00:15:50,120 --> 00:15:50,870
Yes.

388
00:15:50,870 --> 00:15:53,270
But they only extend
into the subcutaneous tissue.

389
00:15:53,320 --> 00:15:54,960
The fat and muscle aren't even visible.

390
00:15:54,960 --> 00:15:56,600
So why are they ulcerated?

391
00:15:56,670 --> 00:15:59,120
There are extensive contusions
on the surface of the body

392
00:15:59,120 --> 00:16:00,120
and subcutaneous hemorrhage.

393
00:16:00,120 --> 00:16:01,670
There are no open wounds.

394
00:16:01,670 --> 00:16:03,120
The mouth, nose, and neck

395
00:16:03,270 --> 00:16:05,390
show no signs
of strangulation or smothering.

396
00:16:05,440 --> 00:16:07,320
He also wasn't killed by a hammer blow.

397
00:16:08,840 --> 00:16:09,630
Here.

398
00:16:13,720 --> 00:16:16,240
There are numerous
hollow-centered bruises

399
00:16:16,240 --> 00:16:18,320
on the victim's back and buttocks.

400
00:16:18,320 --> 00:16:19,670
Hollow-centered bruising?

401
00:16:20,270 --> 00:16:21,030
What's that?

402
00:16:21,030 --> 00:16:23,550
It's a distinctive type
of bruising caused

403
00:16:23,550 --> 00:16:24,390
by a cylindrical blunt object

404
00:16:24,390 --> 00:16:26,630
striking directly against

405
00:16:26,630 --> 00:16:29,080
skin with abundant soft tissue.

406
00:16:29,790 --> 00:16:30,600
Calipers.

407
00:16:33,030 --> 00:16:35,840
Most of the bruises
are about three centimeters wide.

408
00:16:35,870 --> 00:16:37,120
So they were probably caused

409
00:16:37,120 --> 00:16:39,390
by a cylindrical object
about three centimeters in diameter

410
00:16:39,390 --> 00:16:40,870
through repeated blows.

411
00:16:42,030 --> 00:16:43,790
Then what exactly
was the cause of death?

412
00:16:43,910 --> 00:16:45,790
The cause of death
can't be determined yet.

413
00:16:46,120 --> 00:16:47,840
But for now, we can rule out

414
00:16:47,960 --> 00:16:49,240
death by asphyxia.

415
00:16:49,320 --> 00:16:51,030
He also wasn't killed by a hammer blow.

416
00:16:51,030 --> 00:16:52,750
We'll need an autopsy to determine more.

417
00:17:07,920 --> 00:17:08,720
Zhou,

418
00:17:12,270 --> 00:17:13,160
prepare for the autopsy.

419
00:17:14,200 --> 00:17:15,000
Qin,

420
00:17:15,400 --> 00:17:18,160
what will put you in danger next time?

421
00:17:19,510 --> 00:17:20,400
Stomach cancer?

422
00:17:21,640 --> 00:17:22,480
Or something else?

423
00:17:26,660 --> 00:17:30,300
(Winter 2000)

424
00:17:32,570 --> 00:17:37,090
♪The old walkie-talkie I treasure♪

425
00:17:40,160 --> 00:17:44,940
♪The birthday surprise
you gave me that year♪

426
00:17:47,650 --> 00:17:53,030
♪Its buttons worn
and weathered with time♪

427
00:17:53,560 --> 00:17:58,890
♪Still echoing your words,
"Be brave and keep moving on"♪

428
00:18:00,920 --> 00:18:08,880
♪The old train rolled over
our reluctance to part♪

429
00:18:09,510 --> 00:18:14,560
♪You waved goodbye
and faded into the night♪

430
00:18:16,600 --> 00:18:24,910
♪I used to think
we'd always have more time♪

431
00:18:24,910 --> 00:18:30,760
♪But that goodbye became the last♪

432
00:18:32,220 --> 00:18:40,340
♪I carry the warmth you left behind♪

433
00:18:41,030 --> 00:18:46,070
♪Making my way
through every door in life♪

434
00:18:47,850 --> 00:18:55,890
♪Whenever a train
whistle sounds at night♪

435
00:18:56,170 --> 00:19:03,440
♪I suddenly long to call out to you♪

436
00:19:03,640 --> 00:19:08,050
♪Can you hear me?♪

437
00:19:08,060 --> 00:19:11,850
♪Can you hear me?♪

438
00:19:11,850 --> 00:19:19,310
♪Let the old receiver
carry the words I never said♪

439
00:19:19,310 --> 00:19:27,050
♪I've taken on
both your duty and your love♪

440
00:19:27,380 --> 00:19:32,990
♪This train has no return, and when I
look back, you're no longer waiting♪

441
00:19:34,870 --> 00:19:38,470
♪After all these years♪

442
00:19:40,980 --> 00:19:48,460
♪How I wish I could
talk to you just one more time♪

443
00:19:49,360 --> 00:19:50,660
♪And tell you♪

444
00:19:51,880 --> 00:19:55,150
♪I haven't let you down♪
